opening='The hall coordinator is a senior monastic officer who organizes communal procedure, announcements, seating, and voiced ceremonial cues.'
body='The Revised Baizhang Pure Rules has the hall coordinator prepare paper with the hall office before a ceremony; the Practical Pure Rules places this office among librarian, guest prefect, and attendants according to rank. Another pure-rules contents list groups it with the prior, cook, and work supervisor. In recorded events the officer strikes the announcing mallet for communal attendance, proclaims a written address before the teacher mounts the seat, and is appointed alongside librarian and attendant. Liaoan Qingyu pairs the head seat’s example with the hall coordinator’s vocal leading. Qingman’s comic hall image even sends the wooden hall figure to this officer, who slaps it twice. The Chan-specific deployment is therefore public and procedural: this is the officer whose actions make the assembly’s formal encounter happen, not merely a generic administrator.'
